WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:06.580
Opinions determine our experience of life.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:12.510
More than anything else, our opinions provide
us with who we think we are and how we see

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.320
the world.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.439
As a result, we hold our opinions very tightly,
for we fear that if we lose them, we will

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.970
become void of our identity.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:31.099
We hate few things more in life than having
someone oppose and strip us of an opinion.

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:37.060
When our opinions are challenged and proven
wrong, it often feels as though our identity

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.790
has been weakened and diminished.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.780
But why must this be the case?

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:51.130
It is not our identity that is being challenged,
but merely an extension of it.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.640
Our opinions are like glasses.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:58.670
Through which, we view and discern the world
around us.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:05.291
But just like how overtime the prescription
of one’s glasses may change, so must our

00:01:05.291 --> 00:01:07.800
opinions.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.439
As our understanding of life changes, the
prescription of our opinions must change with

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:15.829
it.

00:01:15.829 --> 00:01:22.270
For another opinion to disprove our own only
serves to benefit us because it gives us the

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:29.670
opportunity to replace our old lenses for
potentially new and improved ones.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:36.460
All the while, our identity as the individual
who is wearing the glasses can remain integral

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.520
and constant.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:46.499
And so, we must learn how to accept and embrace
this process as a positive thing.

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:51.270
More important than having opinions in life,
is having good ones.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.079
Progressive ones.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.369
Sharp ones.

00:01:55.369 --> 00:02:01.719
The only way to possess opinions with such
sharpness is through the willingness to listen

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:11.260
to and consider other opinions with rationality
and objectivity, and see if compared to ours,

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.069
they provide a clearer and improved image
of the world.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:22.349
We should embrace our own opinions and fight
to defend them, but only once we have removed

00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:31.739
our ego from the equation and considered the
opposing opinions with legitimate open-mindedness.

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:38.510
There is very little that any person can be
certain about in this life, and we must self-admit

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:46.390
that we are all merely humans with a constantly
changing and loose grip of reality.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:53.620
We have opinions to help us navigate and create
meaning in life, but we must not let them

00:02:53.620 --> 00:03:01.000
in combination with our ego, sweep us away
into believing that we are able to construe

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.329
an ultimate reality.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:11.219
Just as others have the potential to have
misled opinions, so don’t you.

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:19.200
As we are introduced to new experiences, ideas,
and understandings in life, our opinions must

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.840
change accordingly.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:27.560
And if we are willing to adapt, our identity
can move fluidly with them.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:35.170
Our life will then improve because we will
become able to rationalize and exchange opinions

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:41.340
with others in a cohesive and beneficially
effective way.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:48.540
By slightly detaching your ego and identity
from your opinions, you can embrace the fact

00:03:48.540 --> 00:04:09.680
that you are not always right, and as a result,
you will not always 

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:20.329
be wrong.

